1.  Start the program. 
2.  Create an inorder-threaded binary search tree with nodes and thread pointers. 
3.  Accept the value of the node whose inorder successor is to be found. 
4.  Search for the specified node in the tree. 
5.  If the right pointer is a thread, the pointed node is the inorder successor. 
6.  Otherwise, move to the right child and traverse left until a left thread is encountered. 
7.  Display the inorder successor. If no successor exists, display an appropriate message. 
8.  Stop the program.
